## 1. Why this document exists

PROGRESS and PROJECT merged into PM.oot. Stubs remain so old links and agent habits do not 404. Hard delete deferred.

## 2. Problem statement

Hard deletes break continuity; dual maintenance creates drift. Stubs are soft migration.

## 3. Related work (university + commercial)

- URL redirects / API deprecation notices.
- Package deprecation patterns.
- ADR superseded status.

## 4. Rationale for openOODA

PROGRESS hygiene → PM pin/rails; PROJECT checkboxes → PM DESIGN checklist; one live PM.

## 5. Limits and failure modes

Stubs must stay short. Eventually delete when references die.

## 6. Alternatives considered

Wiki-only, issue-tracker-only, single mega-README, or oral tradition — all fail multi-agent continuity or honesty. Prefer git-versioned markdown with clear roles.

## 7. Reality (honesty)

Stubs active; PM authoritative.

## 8. Open questions

1. Delete criteria?
2. Search inbound references before delete?

## 9. Acceptance criteria

- [ ] Stubs only point to PM.
- [ ] PM linked from SPRINT/TOOLS/site.

